  "style": {
    "name": "The Sunward Gate — Heliarch Neoclassical Triumphal Arch (orange/teal complementary, gold accent)",
    "rationale": "Second pass: I kept the orange/teal/gold palette and rebuilt the whole facade (45 wide by 48 tall) as one connected triumphal block. The piers are 16 wide and solid, and the single arch springs at row 25 with a crown at 31. Changes: (1) The vault is now truly deep, 9 blocks to a copper back wall that has an inner gold-sun doorway. Its side walls carry real recessed coffers: teal ribs over verdigris backs, built by leaving blocks out. The soffit is teal with gold coffer centers. (2) The archivolt is a projecting teal ring with a gold keystone, and the spandrels have copper fields with gold Victory accents. (3) Each pier has an engaged outer pilaster with a verdigris flute and an inner pilaster that frames the arch. No column stands free. (4) The plinth now projects 2 and has framed copper insets with gold studs, so no blank base is left. (5) The sculpture niches are framed in teal with copper fields, sandstone figure groups, gold crowns, torches and shields, and teal pedestals. (6) The relief panels above the impost show a horse and rider in sandstone on copper. (7) The entablature has a teal architrave, a copper frieze with sandstone triglyphs, a top-slab soffit, and a teal cornice overhanging 2. (8) The flat-topped attic sits on a sandstone base course and is split into three teal-framed copper panels, with nine gold shields and a central gold sun, under a red-sandstone slab coping. The silhouette stays a pure rectangle cut only by the arch."
  },
